# 8-Bit Music Box song
# The British Grenadiers - traditional march, on fifes and drums.
# Tune: Kerr's Merry Melodies vol. 3 no. 380 (c. 1880s), via the Traditional Tune
# Archive - public domain. Our arrangement: drum roll-off; the tune AABB with the
# fifes in unison, then AABB again with the second fife in harmony; a held chord
# over a roll and a final beat. Drum parts and harmony are ours.
#
# Also the first song to use both new kinds of instrument:
#   "fife_low"  comes from instruments/field_music.inst (an instrument FILE);
#   "side_drum" is defined right here in the song, below.
format 1
title "The British Grenadiers (fifes & drums)"
tempo 116
time 2/4
key 2
bars 68

# The British side drum: a rope drum, a little brighter and tighter than the
# colonial field drum it is based on.
define_instrument side_drum
based_on field_drum
name "Side Drum"
envelope 0.001 0.2 0 0.05
tone 0.68
gain 0.9
color 200 90 80
end

